# issue: none
# notes: `upsert` and `replace` name an existing entity by its `@key`, so on a type with none (the edge `Knows`) each is `T92`, whose fix writes `insert`, which always creates; nothing executes.

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine
    storage: local-filesystem

--- schema
interface Named { name: String }
node Person implements Named {
    handle: String @key
    name: String
    age: I32?
    city: String?
}
node Company implements Named {
    slug: String @key
    name: String
}
node Doc {
    id: String @key
    title: String
    body: String @index
    year: I32
    tags: [String]
    embedding: Vector(3)?
    payload: Blob?
}
node Collection {
    slug: String @key
    min_docs: I32
}
edge WorksAt: Person -> Company @card(0..1)
edge Knows: Person -> Person
edge Authored: Person -> Doc
edge Cites: Doc -> Doc
edge In: Doc -> Collection

--- seed
{"type":"Person","data":{"handle":"ada","name":"Ada","age":36}}
{"type":"Company","data":{"slug":"acme","name":"Acme"}}

--- mutate
query befriend() { replace Knows { @src: "ada", @dst: "ada" } }

--- expect error: type error: T92: `replace Knows`: `Knows` declares no `@key`

--- mutate
query befriend_again() { upsert Knows { @src: "ada", @dst: "ada" } }

--- expect error: type error: T92: `upsert Knows`: `Knows` declares no `@key`
